Employee: Derek Huang | Role: Engineering Manager (EM, L6) | Location: Austin, TX | Base salary: $248K | Geo-differential applied: 'Austin Tier 2 (-8%)' | Hire date: Sep 2024 | Last comp adjustment: Feb 2026 (annual cycle)

Context from Rippling (Band Configuration, effective Feb 2026):
L6-EM band: $245K-$295K base (SF benchmark) | Geo-differentials: Tier 1 (SF/NYC): 0% | Tier 2 (Austin/Seattle/Denver): -8% | Tier 3 (all other US): -15%

Slack — #people-ops (Jan 18, 2026, 4:55 PM):
@cpo: Heads up team — board approved eliminating geo-differentials effective Q2. We're moving to national bands. Don't communicate yet, just flag anyone whose current comp would fall below the new unified floor.
@jasmine.torres: Got it. Timeline for rollout?
@cpo: April 1 target. Comms go out end of March.
@jasmine.torres: 👍

Slack — #eng-managers (Feb 22, 2026, 10:12 AM):
@derek.huang: Hey @vp.eng — I noticed my band shows $245-$295 but with the -8% that puts my effective ceiling at $271K. A couple of my reports are approaching L6 and I want to understand the ceiling for internal promo offers.
@vp.eng: The geo stuff is going away soon. Don't factor it into promo planning. Think national band.
@derek.huang: Oh nice, when?
@vp.eng: Can't say yet officially but plan for Q2.

Google Doc — 'FY26 Leveling Reorg Proposal' (Draft, last edited Mar 5, 2026):
Section: 'Engineering Management Track'
'Proposal: Collapse L6-EM and L7-EM into single Senior EM band. New band: $270K-$340K. Effective date: TBD (pending comp committee approval).'
[COMMENT by @jasmine.torres, Mar 6]: 'This conflicts with the geo elimination timeline. If geo goes away Apr 1 but reorg isn't until May/June, there's a window where L6-EMs hit the unified $245-$295 band with no differential. Derek Huang would be at $248K — fine. But if reorg lands first, the new Senior EM floor is $270K and he'd need a market adjustment.'
[COMMENT by @cpo, Mar 7]: 'Good catch. Sequence matters. Let's discuss Thursday.'

